# http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inXSDDateTimeStamp
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inXSDDateTimeStamp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inXSDDateTimeStamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#> .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#inXSDDateTimeStamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "in XSD date-time stamp"@en .
# 
# https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultCount
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultCount> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#DragSample> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Adult ticks collected in a drag bout. Distinct from nymphs and larvae, which differ in both host preference and epidemiological importance."@en .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "adult count"@en .
# 
# https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultTicksAttached
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#CaptureEvent> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Presence of attached ticks by life stage at capture. Bridges hosts to the vector layer: an animal carrying ticks links that host individual to the tick populations sampled by drag cloth at the same plot."@en .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#adultTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "adult ticks attached"@en .
# 
# https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#attachedTickCount
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#attachedTickCount> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#attachedTickCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#CaptureEvent> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#attachedTickCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#attachedTickCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Number of attached ticks counted at capture (NEON tickNumber). Recorded on only a small fraction of captures; absence means not counted, not zero."@en .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#attachedTickCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attached tick count"@en .
# 
# https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#distanceToFieldSiteKm
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#distanceToFieldSiteKm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#distanceToFieldSiteKm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#ObservationSite> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#distanceToFieldSiteKm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#distanceToFieldSiteKm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Great-circle distance to the nearest NEON field site. Recorded so that a user can choose a proximity threshold rather than inherit the one used at ingestion."@en .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#distanceToFieldSiteKm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "distance to field site (km)"@en .
# 
# https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#individualCount
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#individualCount> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#individualCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#TickSample> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#individualCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#individualCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Number of tick individuals in the tested subsample. Uniformly 1 in the NEON data examined; retained so that pooled testing, which the source field permits, would be representable without a schema change."@en .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#individualCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "individual count"@en .
# 
# https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvaCount
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvaCount> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvaCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#DragSample> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvaCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvaCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Larval ticks collected in a drag bout. Larvae hatch uninfected, so their host associations determine whether the transmission cycle establishes."@en .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvaCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "larva count"@en .
# 
# https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvalTicksAttached
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvalTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvalTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#CaptureEvent> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvalTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvalTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Whether larval ticks were attached to a captured animal. NEON records presence as Y/N, not as a count; parsing it as an integer silently discards every value."@en .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#larvalTicksAttached> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "larval ticks attached"@en .
# 
# https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#lifeStage
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#lifeStage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#lifeStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#VectorOccurrence> .
