<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#TickSample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A tick specimen collected by drag-cloth sampling at a plot and submitted for pathogen testing, identified by NEON subsampleID. In every NEON record examined (231,892 across 39 sites) individualCount is 1, so a sample is a single tick; the count is retained because the field permits pooling in principle. Unlike a host individual, a tick sample is an environmental sample with no tagged organism, so vector-borne detections attach to place rather than to an animal."@en .
<https://bryantpollard.github.io/neon-epn/ontology#TickSample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tick sample"@en .
